n endless loop or work that can be made smaller, then run again.","codeRun.outputLimit":"Your program printed more than the allowed amount of {stream, select, stderr {error output} other {output}}.","codeRun.outputLimitDetail":"The output below is cut off. Print less, then run again.","codeRun.unavailable":"Code execution is not available right now.","codeRun.unavailableDetail":"{reason, select, notConfigured {Running code is switched off on this server.} runtimeMissing {This language version is not installed on the execution server.} other {The execution server did not respond.}} Your code is kept. Try again in a minute.","codeRun.busy":"The execution server is busy.","codeRun.busyDetail":"Your code is kept. Try again in {seconds} seconds.","codeRun.fact.time":"Run time","codeRun.fact.cpu":"CPU time","codeRun.fact.memory":"Memory","codeRun.fact.exit":"Exit code","codeRun.fact.signal":"Signal","codeRun.fact.language":"Language","codeRun.section.stdout":"Standard output","codeRun.section.stderr":"Error output","codeRun.section.compiler":"Compiler output","codeRunner.editor":"{language} source code","codeRunner.stdin":"Standard input (stdin)","codeRunner.stdinHelp":"Type anything your program reads before you press Run. Input cannot be typed while the program is running.","codeRunner.stdinPlaceholder":"Optional. For example: Ada","codeRunner.run":"Run","codeRunner.cancel":"Cancel","codeRunner.runTooltip":"Run your program ({shortcut})","codeRunner.cancelTooltip":"Stop this run. Your code stays as it is.","codeRunner.running":"Running your program…","codeRunner.cancelled":"Run cancelled. Your code is unchanged.","codeRunner.reset":"Reset to starter","codeRunner.resetTitle":"Reset to the starter program?","codeRunner.resetBody":"Your current code is replaced by the starter program and your saved draft is removed.","codeRunner.resetConfirm":"Reset","codeRunner.resetKeep":"Keep my code","codeRunner.upload":"Upload file","codeRunner.uploadFailed":"{name} could not be read as text.","codeRunner.uploadTooLarge":"{name} is larger than {max} KiB. Choose a smaller file.","codeRunner.download":"Download source","codeRunner.version":"{language} version","codeRunner.versionTooltip":"Choose which version runs your code. Each run uses exactly that version.","codeRunner.draftNote":"Your code is saved in this browser only, until you run it.","codeRunner.resultPlaceholder":"Press Run to see what your program prints, or why it stopped."},"toolId":"devtools.php-compiler","slug":"php-compiler","app":"devtools","category":"compilers","keywords":["php","php compiler","online php","run php","php interpreter","php playground"],"name":"PHP Compiler","description":"Write and run PHP 8.5 code in your browser. Add input, press Run, and read the output or the exact error. Nothing to install.","input":{"kind":"text","label":"PHP code","showLineNumbers":true,"maxLength":65536,"acceptFiles":{"accept":".php,text/plain","maxBytes":65536},"secondary":{"label":"Standard input (stdin)","placeholder":"Optional. For example: Ada"}},"settings":{"fields":{"version":{"kind":"select","label":"Version","help":"Each run uses exactly this version.","default":"8.5","choices":[{"value":"8.5","label":"PHP 8.5"}]}}},"resultStats":"status-only","trigger":{"mode":"manual","actionLabel":"Run"},"capabilities":{"cancel":true,"copy":true,"download":true,"network":true},"workbenchMark":{"text":"PHP","tone":"contrast"},"labels":{"result":"Result","empty":"Press Run to see what your program prints, or why it stopped.","ready":"Your program finished. The result explains what happened.","running":"Running your program…"},"content":{"seoTitle":"Online PHP Compiler — Run PHP 8.5 Code","howToUse":["The editor starts with a small PHP program that reads a name from standard input and greets it, so you can press Run straight away.","Write or paste your PHP code. Anything your program reads from the keyboard goes in the Standard input box before you run it.","Press Run or Ctrl/Cmd+Enter. The result starts with one sentence saying what happened, followed by the output, error output and exit code.","If something goes wrong the message names the cause. Fix your code and run again. Your code is kept in this browser while you work."],"limitations":["This page runs PHP 8.5.12 exactly, so results stay the same until the page is updated.","Each run is stopped after 5 seconds of running time (3 seconds of CPU time), and is limited to 256 MiB of memory and 64 KiB of output.","Source code and input are each limited to 64 KiB. Command-line arguments are not supported.","There is no network access, no way to install packages and no files that last between runs.","Input cannot be typed while the program runs. Put everything it will read in the Standard input box first.","If many people run code at once, the server may ask you to wait a few seconds. Your code is kept when that happens."],"faq":[{"q":"Is my code sent to a server, and is it saved?","a":"Yes, your code and input are sent to Canopy's execution server so it can run the program. It runs once in an isolated sandbox and is not stored. A draft stays in your own browser so a refresh does not lose your work."},{"q":"Which PHP version does this use?","a":"PHP 8.5.12. The version is pinned, so results stay the same until the page is updated."},{"q":"Do I need the opening PHP tag?","a":"Yes. Start the file with <?php. Read input with fgets(STDIN) or stream_get_contents(STDIN)."},{"q":"Why was my program stopped?","a":"Programs that run longer than the time limit, use too much memory or print too much are stopped to keep the service fair. The result tells you which limit was reached."}],"examples":[{"label":"Hello with input","text":"<?php\n$name = trim((string) fgets(STDIN));\necho \"Hello, \" . ($name === \"\" ? \"world\" : $name) . \"!\\n\";\n","secondary":"Ada"}],"relatedToolIds":["devtools.ruby-compiler","devtools.kotlin-compiler","devtools.bash-compiler"]}}$spec$::json, updated_at = now()
  WHERE tool_id = 'devtools.php-compiler' AND spec IS NULL;
UPDATE managed_tools SET spec = $spec${"toolId":"media.png-to-jpg","app":"media","category":"image-conversion","keywords":["png","jpg","jpeg","convert","image","compress","background","flatten"],"name":"PNG to JPG","description":"Convert PNG images to JPG with a chosen background.","input":{"kind":"files","label":"Add PNG images","dropzoneDescription":"PNG · up to 50 files · 25 MB each · processed on this device","accept":"image/png,.png","multiple":true,"engine":"image","maxFiles":50,"maxBytes":26214400,"maxTotalBytes":104857600},"settings":{"fields":{"quality":{"kind":"slider","label":"Quality","help":"JPG is lossy. 80 is a good default; above 90 the file grows fast for little visible gain.","default":80,"min":30,"max":100,"suffix":"%"},"background":{"kind":"color","label":"Background","help":"JPG has no transparency, so transparent pixels are flattened onto this colour.","default":"#ffffff"}}},"trigger":{"mode":"manual","actionLabel":"Convert to JPG"},"capabilities":{"cancel":true,"download":true,"progress":true},"workbenchMark":{"text":"PN2J","tone":"accent"},"labels":{"empty":"Drop up to 50 PNG files (.png, 25 MiB each) to convert them to JPG.","ready":"The PNG files and JPG settings are ready.","running":"Converting PNG files to JPG…"},"messages":{"progress.decodingImage":"Decoding image","progress.encodingImage":"Encoding image","progress.imageComplete":"Image complete","media.image.canvasUnavailable":"This browser cannot create an image canvas.","media.validateMediaSignature.invalidSignature":"The file does not have a supported signature.","media.validateMediaSignature.unsupportedType":"This file type is not supported by this tool.","media.validateMediaSignature.mimeMismatch":"The file contents do not match its reported type.","media.validateMediaSignature.animatedImage":"Animated WebP files are not supported. Choose a static image.","media.validateMediaSignature.imageSequence":"Multi-image HEIC sequences are not supported. Choose a single image.","media.validateImageSelection.noFiles":"Choose at least one image.","media.validateImageSelection.tooManyFiles":"Choose no more than {limit, number} images.","media.validateImageSelection.invalidSize":"A selected file has an invalid size.","media.validateImageSelection.fileTooLarge":"Each image must be 25 MiB or smaller.","media.validateImageSelection.totalTooLarge":"The selected images must total 100 MiB or less.","media.validateDecodedImageDimensions.invalidDimensions":"The image dimensions are invalid.","media.validateDecodedImageDimensions.tooManyPixels":"The decoded image must be 100 megapixels or less.","media.image.unsupportedType":"Choose a supported image file.","media.image.imageSequence":"Multi-image HEIC sequences are not supported.","conversion.action":"Convert to {format}","conversion.running":"Converting images to {format}…","conversion.qualityLabel":"Quality","conversion.qualityHelp":"{format, select, jpg {JPG is lossy. 80 is a good default; above 90 the file grows fast for little visible gain.} other {WebP is encoded lossily here. Raise quality for fine details and sharp text; lower it for smaller files.}}","conversion.backgroundLabel":"Background","conversion.backgroundHelp":"JPG has no transparency, so transparent pixels are flattened onto this colour."},"content":{"howToUse":["Add one or more PNG files. Decoding and encoding both happen in your browser, so nothing is uploaded.","Pick a quality. 80 suits photographs and screenshots; raise it for images with fine text or gradients, lower it when file size matters more than detail.","Choose the background colour. Any transparent area in the PNG is composited onto it, because JPG cannot store an alpha channel.","Run the conversion and download the JPGs. Original pixel dimensions are preserved."],"limitations":["Transparency is lost permanently. Pick the background colour to match wherever the image will sit, or keep the PNG if you still need alpha.","JPG is lossy, so every conversion discards detail. Convert from the original PNG rather than re-converting a JPG.","Flat graphics, logos, and screenshots with sharp edges pick up visible ringing in JPG. PNG or WebP is usually the better output for those.","Each image must be 25 MiB or smaller, up to 50 files per run, and no more than 100 megapixels once decoded."],"faq":[{"q":"Why did my transparent PNG come out with a white box?","a":"That is the background colour being applied. JPG has no transparency, so the alpha channel has to be flattened onto something — change the background setting to match your page."},{"q":"What quality should I use?","a":"80 is the default for good reason. Use 90 or above for print or heavy retouching, and 60–70 only when the file has to be small and the image is a photograph."},{"q":"Is any metadata carried over?","a":"No. The image is decoded to raw pixels and re-encoded, which drops EXIF, GPS, and colour-profile data."}]}}$spec$::json, updated_at = now()
  WHERE tool_id = 'media.png-to-jpg' AND spec IS NULL;
UPDATE managed_tools SET spec = $spec${"toolId":"media.png-to-webp","app":"media","category":"image-conversion","keywords":["png","webp","convert","image","compress","transparency","web","batch"],"name":"PNG to WebP","description":"Convert PNG images to WebP.","input":{"kind":"files","label":"Add PNG images","dropzoneDescription":"PNG · up to 50 files · 25 MB each · processed on this device","accept":"image/png,.png","multiple":true,"engine":"image","maxFiles":50,"maxBytes":26214400,"maxTotalBytes":104857600},"settings":{"fields":{"quality":{"kind":"slider","label":"Quality","help":"WebP is encoded lossily here. Raise it for flat graphics and sharp text, lower it for photographs.","default":80,"min":30,"max":100,"suffix":"%"}}},"trigger":{"mode":"manual","actionLabel":"Convert to WebP"},"capabilities":{"cancel":true,"download":true,"progress":true},"workbenchMark":{"text":"PN2W","tone":"accent"},"labels":{"empty":"Drop up to 50 PNG files (.png, 25 MiB each) to convert them to WebP.","ready":"The PNG files and WebP settings are ready.","running":"Converting PNG files to WebP…"},"messages":{"progress.decodingImage":"Decoding image","progress.encodingImage":"Encoding image","progress.imageComplete":"Image complete","media.image.canvasUnavailable":"This browser cannot create an image canvas.","media.validateMediaSignature.invalidSignature":"The file does not have a supported signature.","media.validateMediaSignature.unsupportedType":"This file type is not supported by this tool.","media.validateMediaSignature.mimeMismatch":"The file contents do not match its reported type.","media.validateMediaSignature.animatedImage":"Animated WebP files are not supported. Choose a static image.","media.validateMediaSignature.imageSequence":"Multi-image HEIC sequences are not supported. Choose a single image.","media.validateImageSelection.noFiles":"Choose at least one image.","media.validateImageSelection.tooManyFiles":"Choose no more than {limit, number} images.","media.validateImageSelection.invalidSize":"A selected file has an invalid size.","media.validateImageSelection.fileTooLarge":"Each image must be 25 MiB or smaller.","media.validateImageSelection.totalTooLarge":"The selected images must total 100 MiB or less.","media.validateDecodedImageDimensions.invalidDimensions":"The image dimensions are invalid.","media.validateDecodedImageDimensions.tooManyPixels":"The decoded image must be 100 megapixels or less.","media.image.unsupportedType":"Choose a supported image file.","media.image.imageSequence":"Multi-image HEIC sequences are not supported.","conversion.action":"Convert to {format}","conversion.running":"Converting images to {format}…","conversion.qualityLabel":"Quality","conversion.qualityHelp":"{format, select, jpg {JPG is lossy. 80 is a good default; above 90 the file grows fast for little visible gain.} other {WebP is encoded lossily here. Raise quality for fine details and sharp text; lower it for smaller files.}}","conversion.backgroundLabel":"Background","conversion.backgroundHelp":"JPG has no transparency, so transparent pixels are flattened onto this colour."},"content":{"howToUse":["Add one or more PNG files. Everything is decoded and re-encoded in your browser, so the images never leave the device.","Pick a quality. Screenshots, logos, and anything with sharp text hold up better at 90 or above; photographs saved as PNG are fine at 80.","Run the conversion and download the WebP files. Transparency is carried across, so a PNG with an alpha channel stays transparent.","Use this to shrink PNG assets for the web: a transparent WebP is usually a fraction of the size of the equivalent PNG."],"limitations":["The WebP is encoded lossily, so a PNG that was a pixel-exact master stops being one. Keep the PNG if you need a lossless source to edit.","Flat colour and hard edges are where lossy encoding shows first. If a converted logo or screenshot looks smeared, raise the quality.","Metadata is not carried over. Decoding to raw pixels drops EXIF, GPS, and colour-profile data.","Each image must be 25 MiB or smaller, up to 50 files per run, and no more than 100 megapixels once decoded."],"faq":[{"q":"Is transparency preserved?","a":"Yes. WebP has an alpha channel, so transparent and semi-transparent pixels survive the conversion unchanged in position and coverage."},{"q":"Can I get a lossless WebP instead?","a":"Not from this tool — the encoder here always runs in lossy mode. Setting quality to 100 gets close but is not bit-exact with the source PNG."},{"q":"Why did my file get bigger?","a":"PNG already compresses tiny images and flat two-colour graphics extremely well. When the source is that small, WebP's container overhead can win."}]}}$spec$::json, updated_at = now()
  WHERE tool_id = 'media.png-to-webp' AND spec IS NULL;
