trl/Cmd+Enter. The result starts with one sentence saying what happened, followed by the output, error output and exit code.","If something goes wrong the message names the cause, including the line of a compile error. Fix your code and run again. Your code is kept in this browser while you work."],"limitations":["This page runs Rust 1.99.1 exactly, so results stay the same until the page is updated.","Each run is stopped after 5 seconds of running time (3 seconds of CPU time); compiling may take up to 15 seconds, and is limited to 256 MiB of memory and 64 KiB of output.","Source code and input are each limited to 64 KiB. Command-line arguments are not supported.","There is no network access, no way to install packages and no files that last between runs.","Input cannot be typed while the program runs. Put everything it will read in the Standard input box first.","If many people run code at once, the server may ask you to wait a few seconds. Your code is kept when that happens."],"faq":[{"q":"Is my code sent to a server, and is it saved?","a":"Yes, your code and input are sent to Canopy's execution server so it can run the program. It runs once in an isolated sandbox and is not stored. A draft stays in your own browser so a refresh does not lose your work."},{"q":"Which Rust version does this use?","a":"Rust 1.99.1. The version is pinned, so results stay the same until the page is updated."},{"q":"Can I use crates from crates.io?","a":"No. Only the Rust standard library is available, because the sandbox has no network access and cargo cannot download crates."},{"q":"Why was my program stopped?","a":"Programs that run longer than the time limit, use too much memory or print too much are stopped to keep the service fair. The result tells you which limit was reached."}],"examples":[{"label":"Hello with input","text":"use std::io;\n\nfn main() {\n    let mut line = String::new();\n    io::stdin().read_line(&mut line).expect(\"failed to read stdin\");\n    let name = line.trim();\n    let name = if name.is_empty() { \"world\" } else { name };\n    println!(\"Hello, {}!\", name);\n}\n","secondary":"Ada"}],"relatedToolIds":["devtools.php-compiler","devtools.ruby-compiler","devtools.kotlin-compiler"]}}$spec$::json, updated_at = now()
